<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21019] DoM mirror split or migrate off DoM changes the file's mtime</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21019</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Splitting off a mirror that has a DoM component (&lt;tt&gt;lfs mirror split -d&lt;/tt&gt;, or &lt;tt&gt;LL_LEASE_LAYOUT_SPLIT&lt;/tt&gt;) sets the file's mtime to the time of the split. &lt;tt&gt;lfs migrate&lt;/tt&gt; of a DoM file to a layout without DoM does the same. A split of a mirror without DoM keeps the mtime. Tools that release the flash mirror of cold files change the mtime of every file they release, and backups see them as modified.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Reproducer"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Reproducer&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ldiskfs MDT, two OSTs:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-bash"&gt;
lfs setstripe -E 64K -L mdt -E eof -c 1 f
dd &lt;span class="code-object"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt;=/dev/urandom of=f bs=128K count=1
touch -d &lt;span class="code-quote-red"&gt;"2020-01-01 12:00"&lt;/span&gt; f
lfs mirror extend -N -c 1 f
lfs mirror split -d --mirror-id=1 f
stat -c %Y f    &lt;span class="code-comment"&gt;# the &lt;span class="code-object"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt; of the split, not 1577876400&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Cause"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Cause&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;mdd_dom_fixup()&lt;/tt&gt; punches the DoM data on the MDT. &lt;tt&gt;ldiskfs_truncate()&lt;/tt&gt; updates the times with &lt;tt&gt;i_mtime = i_ctime = current_time()&lt;/tt&gt;, which for the NOCMTIME inodes of osd-ldiskfs (ext4-nocmtime.patch) copies the ctime into the mtime. Since &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-10048" title="osd-ldiskfs to truncate outside of main transaction" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-10048"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-10048&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; the truncate runs from &lt;tt&gt;osd_trans_stop()&lt;/tt&gt; after the punch transaction, so it also replaces the mtime a caller set in that transaction. osd-zfs changes no times on a punch. &lt;tt&gt;lfs&lt;/tt&gt; restores no times around a split (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14508" title="lfs mirror operations do not preserve timestamps" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-14508"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-14508&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; covers extend and resync only), and a restore in userspace after the split races with writes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Fix"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Fix&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A truncate in ldiskfs should not change the times of Lustre's NOCMTIME inodes: the caller sets the times it wants in the punch transaction, as on osd-zfs. Test: &lt;tt&gt;sanity-flr&lt;/tt&gt; test_61d.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Related: &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14508" title="lfs mirror operations do not preserve timestamps" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-14508"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-14508&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15557" title="creating/breaking mirror should not change file timestamps" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-15557"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-15557&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-10048" title="osd-ldiskfs to truncate outside of main transaction" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-10048"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-10048&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment>ldiskfs MDT with DoM</environment>
